{
  "credit": "Skyport - Airport Station. A console with the map surface sunk into a raised bezel. Every face samples the patch of texture that lies where it sits, so the pieces reconstruct one continuous surface instead of each wearing a copy: the walls take rows 2-16 and the bezel the two rows above them, and each bezel's TOP samples the texture in plan - north rows 0-3, west columns 0-3 - so the brass edging turns the corner onto the top of the block and meets the brass line running along the wall below it. Give a piece the whole texture instead and a full 16px panel is squashed into a 2px band. Only the sunken floor shows the map screen, or the screen appears five times.",
